// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
// survey.py's arguments and help (mise run text:survey --help). mise rewraps the help to the
// terminal but keeps its line breaks: a paragraph, or a list's item, is one line.

long_about """
    text:compare over a sample of the corpus: which differences from EUR-Lex are rules of ours to fix.

    EUR-Lex's HTML is made from Formex by rules, so a difference that many texts have is one rule, ours or theirs, and one that only one text has is a quirk of its source. text:compare finds the differences on one page; this finds which are general.

    1. The sample: the mirror's (corpus:fetch) acts as published (CELEX 3…) and consolidated versions (0…), stratified by kind, Formex version and type of act (regulation, directive, decision, other), spread across sizes within each stratum, one version of an act at most. Chosen by the manifestations' Cellar IDs, so the same mirror gives the same sample.
    2. Each converted (convert_texts) and rendered as the viewer renders it (render_texts), without a database or Cellar: text-compare/survey/{legal-text,pages}.
    3. Each page compared with EUR-Lex's HTML of the text, as text:compare compares (its reference is fetched from Cellar once, into text-compare/reference/).
    4. text-compare/survey/summary.md: the patterns, ranked by how many texts have them, with examples from several texts; then each text's count. Each text's every difference is in text-compare/reports/{celex}.md.
    """

flag "--language <code>" default="ENG" help="The mirror's language (see corpus:fetch)"
flag "--size <n>" default="200" help="How many texts to sample"
flag "--compare-only" help="Compare the pages the last run rendered, without sampling or converting again"

example "mise run text:survey" header="Survey a sample of the corpus" help="200 English texts"
example "mise run text:survey --size 50 --language FRA" header="Survey another language" help="50 French texts"
example "mise run text:survey --compare-only" header="Rerun comparison" help="Compare without sampling or converting again"
